{
  "title": "Fourier transform",
  "slug": "fourier-transform",
  "hue": 275,
  "lede": "The Fourier transform rewrites any signal as a sum of sine waves, turning a wave over time into a recipe of frequencies.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "experience",
      "heading": "Draw a wave, see its sines",
      "body": "<style>\n.ft{box-sizing:border-box;max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;font-family:var(--ow-font);color:var(--ow-fg);--orig:color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-muted) 55%,transparent);--off:color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-line) 85%,var(--ow-muted))}\n.ft *{box-sizing:border-box}\n.ft-top{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px 18px;margin-bottom:12px}\n.ft-q{margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;font-weight:600;flex:1 1 300px}\n.ft-q b{color:var(--ow-accent)}\n.ft-chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}\n.ft-chip{appearance:none;font:inherit;font-size:14px;min-height:40px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:999px;border:1.5px solid var(--ow-line);background:var(--ow-bg);color:var(--ow-fg);cursor:pointer;touch-action:manipulation}\n.ft-chip[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:var(--ow-fg);border-color:var(--ow-fg);color:var(--ow-bg)}\n.ft button:focus-visible,.ft input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-accent) 55%,transparent);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:8px}\n.ft-pane{border-radius:16px;background:var(--ow-panel);border:1px solid var(--ow-line);padding:10px 14px 8px}\n.ft-pane+.ft-pane{margin-top:10px}\n.ft-h{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:2px 10px;margin:0;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.ft-h>span:last-child{text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-weight:500}\n.ft-leg{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-left:12px}\n.ft-leg i{display:inline-block;width:16px;height:3px;border-radius:2px}\n.ft svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none}\n.ft-wave{touch-action:none;cursor:crosshair}\n.ft svg text{font-family:var(--ow-font);font-size:11px;fill:var(--ow-muted)}\n.ft-spec{cursor:pointer;touch-action:none}\n.ft-ctl{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-top:12px}\n.ft-play{appearance:none;flex:none;width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;border:0;background:var(--ow-accent);color:var(--ow-accent-ink);cursor:pointer;display:grid;place-items:center;touch-action:manipulation}\n.ft-play svg{width:18px;height:18px}\n.ft-ctl>div{flex:1;min-width:0}\n.ft-lab{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;font-size:15px;font-weight:600}\n.ft-lab output{white-space:nowrap;font-family:var(--ow-mono);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ow-muted);font-weight:500}\n.ft input[type=range]{width:100%;margin:6px 0 0;height:28px;accent-color:var(--ow-accent);cursor:pointer}\n.ft-chips .ft-chip{flex:none}\n@media (max-width:420px){.ft-q{font-size:17px}.ft-chips{gap:6px}.ft-chip{padding:6px 10px;font-size:13.5px;min-height:38px}.ft-pane{padding:8px 10px 6px}.ft-leg{margin-left:6px}}\n</style>\n<div class=\"ft\">\n  <div class=\"ft-top\">\n    <p class=\"ft-q\"><b>Draw any wave</b> in the box, or pick one. The bars show how much of each sine is inside it.</p>\n    <div class=\"ft-chips\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Pick a wave\">\n      <button class=\"ft-chip\" type=\"button\" data-w=\"square\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Square</button>\n      <button class=\"ft-chip\" type=\"button\" data-w=\"saw\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Sawtooth</button>\n      <button class=\"ft-chip\" type=\"button\" data-w=\"chirp\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Chirp</button>\n      <button class=\"ft-chip\" type=\"button\" data-w=\"flat\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Blank</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ft-pane\">\n    <p class=\"ft-h\"><span>The wave</span><span><span class=\"ft-leg\"><i style=\"background:var(--orig)\"></i>yours</span><span class=\"ft-leg\"><i style=\"background:var(--ow-accent)\"></i>rebuilt from sines</span></span></p>\n    <svg class=\"ft-wave\" id=\"ft-w\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 180\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The wave and its rebuild from sines. Drag to draw.\"></svg>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ft-pane\">\n    <p class=\"ft-h\"><span>Its sines</span><span id=\"ft-m\"></span></p>\n    <svg class=\"ft-spec\" id=\"ft-s\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Spectrum: strength of each harmonic\"></svg>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ft-ctl\">\n    <button class=\"ft-play\" type=\"button\" id=\"ft-go\" aria-label=\"Add sines one by one\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path id=\"ft-ic\" d=\"M5 3l12 7-12 7z\"/></svg></button>\n    <div>\n      <label class=\"ft-lab\" for=\"ft-n\"><span>Sines used to rebuild</span><output id=\"ft-no\" for=\"ft-n\"></output></label>\n      <input id=\"ft-n\" type=\"range\" min=\"1\" max=\"32\" step=\"1\" value=\"5\">\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var M=256,K=32,NS='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg',x=new Float64Array(M),A=new Float64Array(K+1),B=new Float64Array(K+1);\n  var cosT=[],sinT=[];for(var k=0;k<=K;k++){var c=new Float64Array(M),s=new Float64Array(M);for(var n=0;n<M;n++){c[n]=Math.cos(2*Math.PI*k*n/M);s[n]=Math.sin(2*Math.PI*k*n/M)}cosT.push(c);sinT.push(s)}\n  var W=document.getElementById('ft-w'),SP=document.getElementById('ft-s'),R=document.getElementById('ft-n'),no=document.getElementById('ft-no'),meta=document.getElementById('ft-m');\n  var reduce=window.matchMedia&&window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;\n  var shapes={\n    square:function(t){return t<.5?.8:-.8},\n    saw:function(t){return .8-1.6*t},\n    chirp:function(t){return .8*Math.sin(2*Math.PI*(1.5*t+9*t*t))},\n    flat:function(){return 0}\n  };\n  function load(name){for(var n=0;n<M;n++)x[n]=shapes[name](n/M);dft()}\n  function dft(){for(var k=0;k<=K;k++){var a=0,b=0,c=cosT[k],s=sinT[k];for(var n=0;n<M;n++){a+=x[n]*c[n];b+=x[n]*s[n]}A[k]=a;B[k]=b}}\n  function mag(k){return(k?2:1)*Math.sqrt(A[k]*A[k]+B[k]*B[k])/M}\n  function rebuild(N,only){var y=new Float64Array(M);for(var n=0;n<M;n++){var v=only?0:A[0]/M;for(var k=only||1;k<=(only||N);k++)v+=2/M*(A[k]*cosT[k][n]+B[k]*sinT[k][n]);y[n]=v}return y}\n  function el(n,a){var e=document.createElementNS(NS,n);for(var key in a)e.setAttribute(key,a[key]);return e}\n  var w=640,H=180,SH=120,pad=8;\n  function size(){w=Math.max(260,Math.round(W.getBoundingClientRect().width)||640);H=w<480?150:180;SH=w<480?104:120;W.setAttribute('viewBox','0 0 '+w+' '+H);SP.setAttribute('viewBox','0 0 '+w+' '+SH)}\n  function X(n){return pad+(w-2*pad)*n/(M-1)}function Y(v){return H/2-v*(H/2-12)}\n  function path(y){var d='';for(var n=0;n<M;n++)d+=(n?'L':'M')+X(n).toFixed(1)+' '+Y(Math.max(-1.3,Math.min(1.3,y[n]))).toFixed(1);return d}\n  function draw(){\n    var N=+R.value;no.textContent=N+(N===1?' sine':' sines');R.setAttribute('aria-valuetext',N+' sines');\n    while(W.firstChild)W.removeChild(W.firstChild);\n    W.appendChild(el('line',{x1:pad,x2:w-pad,y1:H/2,y2:H/2,stroke:'var(--ow-line)','stroke-width':1}));\n    var top=null;for(var k=N;k>=1;k--)if(mag(k)>.02){top=k;break}\n    if(top)W.appendChild(el('path',{d:path(rebuild(N,top)),fill:'none',stroke:'var(--ow-accent)','stroke-width':1.2,'stroke-dasharray':'3 4',opacity:.6}));\n    W.appendChild(el('path',{d:path(x),fill:'none',stroke:'var(--orig)','stroke-width':5,'stroke-linejoin':'round','stroke-linecap':'round'}));\n    var y=rebuild(N);W.appendChild(el('path',{d:path(y),fill:'none',stroke:'var(--ow-accent)','stroke-width':2.5,'stroke-linejoin':'round'}));\n    if(top){var t=el('text',{x:w-pad,y:H-4,'text-anchor':'end'});t.textContent='dashed: sine #'+top+' alone';W.appendChild(t)}\n    var err=0,tot=0;for(var n=0;n<M;n++){err+=(x[n]-y[n])*(x[n]-y[n]);tot+=x[n]*x[n]}\n    meta.textContent=tot>1e-6?'rebuild holds '+Math.max(0,Math.min(100,Math.floor(100*(1-err/tot))))+'% of the energy':'draw something';\n    while(SP.firstChild)SP.removeChild(SP.firstChild);\n    var mx=0;for(k=1;k<=K;k++)mx=Math.max(mx,mag(k));\n    var bw=(w-2*pad)/K,base=SH-18;\n    SP.appendChild(el('line',{x1:pad,x2:w-pad,y1:base+.5,y2:base+.5,stroke:'var(--ow-line)','stroke-width':1}));\n    for(k=1;k<=K;k++){var h=mx>1e-9?Math.max(1.5,(base-6)*mag(k)/mx):1.5;SP.appendChild(el('rect',{x:(pad+(k-1)*bw+bw*.18).toFixed(1),y:(base-h).toFixed(1),width:(bw*.64).toFixed(1),height:h.toFixed(1),rx:Math.min(3,bw*.2).toFixed(1),fill:k<=N?'var(--ow-accent)':'var(--off)'}))}\n    [1,8,16,24,32].forEach(function(k){var t=el('text',{x:pad+(k-.5)*bw,y:SH-3,'text-anchor':'middle'});t.textContent=k;SP.appendChild(t)});\n  }\n  var chips=[].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.ft-chip'));\n  function pick(name){chips.forEach(function(b){b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b.getAttribute('data-w')===name))})}\n  chips.forEach(function(b){b.addEventListener('click',function(){pick(b.getAttribute('data-w'));load(b.getAttribute('data-w'));draw()})});\n  R.addEventListener('input',function(){stop();draw()});\n  // Drawing: each move writes the samples between the last and this pointer position.\n  var drawing=false,lastN=-1,lastV=0;\n  function at(e){var b=W.getBoundingClientRect(),px=(e.clientX-b.left)/b.width*w,py=(e.clientY-b.top)/b.height*H;return{n:Math.max(0,Math.min(M-1,Math.round((px-pad)/(w-2*pad)*(M-1)))),v:Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,(H/2-py)/(H/2-12)))}}\n  function paint(p){if(lastN<0){x[p.n]=p.v}else{var a=Math.min(lastN,p.n),b=Math.max(lastN,p.n);for(var n=a;n<=b;n++){var f=b===a?1:(n-lastN)/(p.n-lastN);x[n]=lastV+(p.v-lastV)*f}}lastN=p.n;lastV=p.v;dft();draw()}\n  W.addEventListener('pointerdown',function(e){e.preventDefault();drawing=true;stop();pick('');lastN=-1;W.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);paint(at(e))});\n  W.addEventListener('pointermove',function(e){if(drawing)paint(at(e))});\n  W.addEventListener('pointerup',function(){drawing=false});W.addEventListener('pointercancel',function(){drawing=false});\n  // Click or drag on the bars to choose how many sines rebuild the wave.\n  var specDrag=false;\n  function fromSpec(e){var b=SP.getBoundingClientRect(),px=(e.clientX-b.left)/b.width*w;R.value=Math.max(1,Math.min(K,Math.ceil((px-pad)/((w-2*pad)/K))));stop();draw()}\n  SP.addEventListener('pointerdown',function(e){e.preventDefault();specDrag=true;SP.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);fromSpec(e)});\n  SP.addEventListener('pointermove',function(e){if(specDrag)fromSpec(e)});\n  SP.addEventListener('pointerup',function(){specDrag=false});\n  var timer=0,go=document.getElementById('ft-go'),ic=document.getElementById('ft-ic');\n  function stop(){if(timer){clearInterval(timer);timer=0}ic.setAttribute('d','M5 3l12 7-12 7z');go.setAttribute('aria-label','Add sines one by one')}\n  go.addEventListener('click',function(){\n    if(timer){stop();return}\n    if(reduce){R.value=+R.value>=K?1:K;draw();return}\n    R.value=1;draw();ic.setAttribute('d','M5 3h3.5v14H5zM11.5 3H15v14h-3.5z');go.setAttribute('aria-label','Pause');\n    timer=setInterval(function(){if(+R.value>=K){stop();return}R.value=+R.value+1;draw()},160);\n  });\n  window.addEventListener('resize',function(){size();draw()});\n  load('square');size();draw();\n})();\n</script>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "Every signal is a sum of sines",
      "body": "The Fourier transform takes a function and returns another that describes how much of each frequency is present in it [1], like decomposing a musical chord into the intensities of its pitches [2]. That output is the frequency domain representation [3]. In 1822 Joseph Fourier claimed that any function, continuous or not, can be expanded into a series of sines [4]. Or, in BetterExplained's words: given a smoothie, it finds the recipe [5].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "outputs another function that describes the extent to which various frequencies are present in the original function"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The Fourier transform is analogous to decomposing the sound of a musical chord into the intensities of its constituent pitches."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "the output of the operation is sometimes called the frequency domain representation of the original function"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "that any function, whether continuous or discontinuous, can be expanded into a series of sines"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://betterexplained.com/articles/an-interactive-guide-to-the-fourier-transform/",
          "title": "An Interactive Guide to the Fourier Transform (BetterExplained)",
          "quote": "Given a smoothie, it finds the recipe."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "DFT and FFT, one sentence each",
      "body": "The discrete Fourier transform (DFT) turns a finite list of samples into a list of the same length giving the amplitude and phase of each frequency [1]. The fast Fourier transform (FFT) computes the same DFT by factoring its matrix into sparse pieces [2], cutting the time to O(n log n) [3]. James Cooley and John Tukey published the general FFT in 1965 [4], though Gauss had a very similar method in unpublished 1805 work [5]; Gilbert Strang called it the most important numerical algorithm of our lifetime [6].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discrete_Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Discrete Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "converts a finite sequence of numbers into another sequence of the same length, representing the amplitude and phase of different frequency components"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast_Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fast Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "An FFT rapidly computes such transformations by factorizing the DFT matrix into a product of sparse (mostly zero) factors."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooley%E2%80%93Tukey_FFT_algorithm",
          "title": "Cooley-Tukey FFT algorithm (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "to reduce the computation time to O(n log n)"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast_Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fast Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "James Cooley and John Tukey independently rediscovered these earlier algorithms and published a more general FFT in 1965"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast_Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fast Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "his method was very similar to the one that would be published in 1965 by James Cooley and John Tukey"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast_Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fast Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "the most important numerical algorithm of our lifetime"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "figure",
      "heading": "Three sines make a square",
