    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "Where it is used",
      "body": "Audio: splitting a sound into its pitches is the textbook picture [1]. Fast cosine transforms, close cousins, run JPEG and MP3 encoding and decoding [2]; JPEG applies one to each 8×8 block of pixels [3], because a DCT, like a Fourier transform, produces a spatial frequency spectrum [4]. The Fourier transform is also used in magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) [5].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "decomposing the sound of a musical chord into the intensities of its constituent pitches"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast_Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fast Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "fast DCT used for JPEG and MPEG/MP3 encoding and decoding"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPEG",
          "title": "JPEG (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "each of the Y, Cb, and Cr data undergoes the discrete cosine transform (DCT)"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPEG",
          "title": "JPEG (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "A DCT is similar to a Fourier transform in the sense that it produces a kind of spatial frequency spectrum."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_transform",
          "title": "Fourier transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The Fourier transform is also used in magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)"
        }
      ]
    }
